  "body": " How many roots does the function have?  To show that there are exactly roots, you need to not only show that exist, but also that there are not more than .     By inspection, we see is a root of . The question now is whether there could possibly be other roots. Since is differentiable over all real numbers, if there is another root , then by Rolle's Theorem, for some strictly between and . However, is never zero. So, there is no second root: has precisely one root.  "
