  "body": "2015Q  Two tall sticks are vertically planted into the ground, separated by a distance of cm. We simultaneously put two snails at the base of each stick. The two snails then begin to climb their respective sticks. The first snail is moving with a speed of cm per minute, while the second snail is moving with a speed of cm per minute. What is the rate of change of the distance between the two snails when the first snail reaches cm above the ground?  You'll want to think about the difference in height of the two snails.   cm per minute    We compute the distance between the two snails after minutes as where is the altitude of the first snail, and the altitude of the second snail after minutes.  We differentiate the above equation with respect to and get   We are told that and . It will take minutes for the first snail to reach , and in this time the second snail will reach .  At this point , hence .  Therefore     "
