  "body": "Warming iced tea  The temperature of a glass of iced tea is initially . After 5 minutes, the tea has heated to in a room where the air temperature is .  Determine the temperature as a function of time.  What is the temperature after 10 minutes?  Determine when the tea will reach a temperature of .     Solution Part (a)  Denote by the temperature of the tea minutes after it was removed from the fridge, and let be the ambient temperature.  By Newton's law of cooling, for some, as yet unknown, constant of proportionality .  By Corollary , since the initial temperature .  This solution is not complete because it still contains an unknown constant, namely . We have not yet used the given data that . We can use it to determine . At ,     Part (b)  To find the temperature at 10 minutes we can just use the solution we have determined above.     Part (c)  We can find when the temperature is by solving :     "
