  "number": "3.3.4.1",
  "title": "",
  "body": " Which of the following is a differential equation for an unknown function of ?    Review the definition of a differential equation at the beginning of this section.  (a), (b)  In the beginning of this section, the text says A differential equation is an equation for an unknown function that involves the derivative of the unknown function. Our unknown function is , so a differential equation is an equation that relates and . This applies to (a) and (b), but not (c), (d), or (e).  Note that : this is the derivative of with respect to .  "
